---
import Divider from "../../../../components/ui/Divider.astro";
import Layout from "../../../../layouts/Layout.astro";
import { Code } from "astro-expressive-code/components";

//#region CodeSnippets
const P1 = `scores ← [88, 42, 95, 60, 71]

PROCEDURE countAbove(aList, limit)
{
  found ← 0
  i ← 1

  REPEAT UNTIL(i > LENGTH(aList))
  {
    IF(aList[i] > limit)
    {
      found ← found + 1
    }
    i ← i + 1
  }

  RETURN(found)
}

DISPLAY(countAbove(scores, 65))`;

const P2 = `PROCEDURE halve(n)
{
  steps ← 0
  left ← n

  REPEAT UNTIL(left = 0)
  {
    steps ← steps + 1
    left ← (left - (left MOD 2)) / 2
  }

  RETURN(steps)
}`;

const P3 = `PROCEDURE grid(n)
{
  total ← 0
  i ← 1

  REPEAT UNTIL(i > n)
  {
    j ← 1

    REPEAT UNTIL(j > n)
    {
      total ← total + 1
      j ← j + 1
    }

    i ← i + 1
  }

  RETURN(total)
}`;

const Prompt = `WRITTEN RESPONSE 2(a)

  Identify the number of times the body of the
  iteration statement will execute.

  AND describe a condition or error that would
  cause an infinite loop.`;
//#endregion
---

<Layout>
  <div class="container my-4">
    <div class="row justify-content-center">
      <div class="col-sm-12 col-md-10">
        <a href="/courses/ap-csp/" class="btn btn-sm btn-outline-light mb-3">
          <i class="si-arrow-left"></i> Back
        </a>

        <h1>Written Response Rehearsal: The Loop</h1>

        <h4 class="text-sn-theme">
          Three problems &middot; on paper &middot; this is Written Response 2(a)
        </h4>

        <Divider variant="8" classes="mb-5" />

        <section id="objective">
          <h2>Objective</h2>

          <p>
            <b>This is one of your six Create Task points, rehearsed on somebody
            else's code.</b> In May you will answer it about your own program, with
            only your Project Reference in front of you.
          </p>

          <Code code={Prompt} frame="code" lang="txt" title="The Real Prompt" showLineNumbers={false} class="my-3" />

          <p>
            <b>Notice the word <i>and</i>.</b> Both halves or nothing &mdash; a
            correct count with no infinite-loop answer scores the same as a blank
            page.
          </p>

          <p>
            <b>These are in exam notation on purpose.</b> Your own program is in
            JavaScript, but the exam's multiple-choice questions use the reference
            sheet, and counting is counting. If the notation slows you down, that is
            the thing to fix before May.
          </p>

          <p class="text-body-secondary">
            <b>Paper only. Do not run these.</b>
          </p>
        </section>

        <Divider variant="8" classes="my-5" />

        <section id="problems">
          <h2>The Problems</h2>

          <hr class="my-4" />

          <h3>Problem 1</h3>

          <Code code={P1} frame="code" lang="txt" title="countAbove" showLineNumbers={false} class="mb-3" />

          <ol>
            <li><b>How many times does the loop body execute?</b></li>
            <li><b>What does the program display?</b> Be exact.</li>
            <li>Describe <b>one change</b> that would make this loop run forever, and say why it never stops.</li>
            <li>
              Now a harder one. <b>Without changing the loop at all</b>, describe a
              value of <code>aList</code> that makes the body execute{" "}
              <b>zero</b> times.
            </li>
          </ol>

          <hr class="my-4" />

          <h3>Problem 2</h3>

          <Code code={P2} frame="code" lang="txt" title="halve" showLineNumbers={false} class="mb-3" />

          <ol>
            <li>
              <b>How many times does the body execute</b> for each of these?{" "}
              <code>halve(20)</code>, <code>halve(7)</code>,{" "}
              <code>halve(1)</code>, <code>halve(0)</code>.
            </li>
            <li>One of those four is worth pausing on. Which, and why?</li>
            <li>
              Someone replaces <code>left &larr; (left - (left MOD 2)) / 2</code>{" "}
              with <code>left &larr; left / 2</code>. <b>The loop now runs
              forever.</b> Explain precisely why &mdash; the answer is not
              &quot;because it is wrong.&quot;
            </li>
          </ol>

          <hr class="my-4" />

          <h3>Problem 3</h3>

          <Code code={P3} frame="code" lang="txt" title="grid" showLineNumbers={false} class="mb-3" />

          <ol>
            <li><b>How many times does the inner body execute</b> for <code>grid(3)</code>, <code>grid(4)</code>, and <code>grid(5)</code>?</li>
            <li>
              <b>There are two loops here.</b> Written Response 2(a) asks about the{" "}
              <b>first iteration statement</b>. Which one is that, and how many
              times does <i>its</i> body execute for <code>grid(4)</code>?
            </li>
            <li>
              Someone moves <code>j &larr; 1</code> so that it sits <b>above</b> the
              outer loop instead of inside it. <b>What does <code>grid(4)</code>{" "}
              return now?</b> Explain what happened.
            </li>
          </ol>

          <hr class="my-4" />

          <h3>Then: Your Own</h3>

          <p>
            <b>Find the first loop inside a procedure in your own program.</b> Write
            out an answer to Written Response 2(a) about it &mdash; both halves, in
            full sentences.
          </p>

          <p>
            <b class="text-sn-theme">If you cannot find a loop inside one of your own
            procedures, that is the most useful thing this page will tell you.</b>{" "}
            You have sessions left to fix it.
          </p>
        </section>

        <Divider variant="8" classes="my-5" />

        <section id="submit">
          <h2>Submit</h2>

          <p>
            All three problems answered, plus your own Written Response 2(a) in full
            sentences.
          </p>

          <p>Worth <b>5 points</b>, graded on completion.</p>
        </section>

        <h1 class="text-center mt-5 text-sn-theme border border-primary slow-flash">
          Commence Challenge
        </h1>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</Layout>
